   "start_page": 136,
   "summary": "This subfile comprises the concluding annexes to Despatch No. 5601, the Embassy's monthly report on conditions in Japan for April 1941. It contains telegrams Nos. 539 through 619 sent between April 11 and April 30, 1941, recording communications on the Soviet-Japanese Neutrality Pact, the Tripartite Pact, Japanese southward advance rumors, bombing of mission properties in China, and visa and personnel matters. It also includes the complete monthly list of despatches Nos. 5476 through 5555 forwarded during April 1941, detailing diplomatic reporting on Japanese security laws, military damages in China, the Tripartite Alliance, and economic reports.",
   "title": "Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of April 1941 [Concluding Lists of Telegrams and Despatches]",
   "to": "Cordell Hull, Secretary of State"
  },
  {
   "about": "Comprehensive monthly report on political, economic, diplomatic, and military conditions in Japan during May 1941, transmitted by Ambassador Joseph C. Grew.",
