   "start_page": 191,
   "summary": "This subfile contains a duplicate record copy of Despatch No. 5682 sent by Ambassador Joseph C. Grew to the Secretary of State, including the cover transmittal sheet, distribution list to other diplomatic posts, table of contents, and the first twelve pages of Report No. 1676. The report text covers Japanese-American relations during May 1941, detailing Grew's conferences with Foreign Minister Matsuoka over Article 3 of the Tripartite Pact and American convoy policies, formal representations regarding bombings of American property in China and abrogation of the Fur Seal Convention, and Japanese press reactions to statements by President Roosevelt, Secretary Hull, and Senator Claude Pepper. The document ends abruptly on page 206 in the middle of a sentence regarding the China Incident.",
   "title": "Despatch No. 5682: Report of Conditions in Japan During the Month of May 1941 [Duplicate Copy]",
